WEBVTT

00:00:24.810 --> 00:00:25.940
Meat?

00:00:26.810 --> 00:00:29.570
I found an animal that even I could catch.

00:00:29.650 --> 00:00:31.610
The early bird gets the worm, as they say.

00:00:32.610 --> 00:00:33.650
Please have some.

00:00:33.740 --> 00:00:35.320
Wow! Thanks so much.

00:00:36.160 --> 00:00:37.410
Delicious!

00:00:37.490 --> 00:00:38.700
Hana, you should have some too.

00:00:38.780 --> 00:00:39.780
Looks good.

00:00:39.950 --> 00:00:41.750
It's very tender.

00:00:42.040 --> 00:00:43.160
And it doesn't smell funny.

00:00:44.500 --> 00:00:45.540
Yummy!

00:00:45.750 --> 00:00:47.420
Are there more of this animal around?

00:00:48.000 --> 00:00:50.340
Yes, I saw a number of them.

00:00:52.960 --> 00:00:54.010
Now I feel motivated!

00:00:54.590 --> 00:00:55.510
Thanks so much, Chisa.

00:00:56.090 --> 00:00:57.510
I'm gathering firewood again today.

00:00:58.010 --> 00:01:01.220
Okay, then I'll hunt for something big.

00:02:32.060 --> 00:02:33.110
GREATER COLD

00:02:33.190 --> 00:02:35.400
Maybe I should make another boomerang.

00:02:41.570 --> 00:02:42.570
You guys.

00:02:44.620 --> 00:02:45.950
What's wrong?

00:02:46.160 --> 00:02:48.330
Where's the other one, the smallest one?

00:02:49.040 --> 00:02:50.580
Did it get attacked by something?

00:02:51.210 --> 00:02:52.500
Wait...

00:02:52.830 --> 00:02:54.750
<i>No way! The animal I just ate...</i>

00:03:00.630 --> 00:03:03.010
No, I didn't mean...

00:03:13.520 --> 00:03:15.900
Just go! Get far away!

00:03:15.980 --> 00:03:18.110
Don't ever get near me again!

00:03:24.950 --> 00:03:30.040
<i>I said they weren't pets or livestock,
but I let them stay with me.</i>

00:03:31.210 --> 00:03:35.380
<i>They let their guard down because of me
and ended up getting caught easily.</i>

00:03:36.130 --> 00:03:39.380
<i>If they were so important, I should have
protected them like they were my own!</i>

00:03:39.460 --> 00:03:41.630
<i>This happened because I didn't do my best!</i>

00:03:43.590 --> 00:03:45.850
<i>Don't puke! You already ate it!</i>

00:03:45.930 --> 00:03:48.100
<i>It's been eaten! Let it nourish you!</i>

00:03:51.060 --> 00:03:53.100
<i>I'm glad that I didn't...</i>

00:03:53.560 --> 00:03:54.690
<i>give them names.</i>

00:03:59.150 --> 00:04:01.190
Rest up. I'll go look up ahead.

00:04:01.400 --> 00:04:02.780
Right. I'm going too.

00:04:04.610 --> 00:04:06.530
Those guys sure have lots of stamina.

00:04:07.030 --> 00:04:09.660
My legs and arms are shaking.

00:04:09.740 --> 00:04:11.620
They said they had prepared for this.

00:04:12.210 --> 00:04:14.420
They studied and trained for this.

00:04:15.380 --> 00:04:19.800
They went through unimaginable trials,
and they take the lead even now.

00:04:20.550 --> 00:04:21.710
They're amazing.

00:04:21.800 --> 00:04:22.840
Darn you, Arashi!

00:04:23.420 --> 00:04:24.760
You just up and disappeared on us!

00:04:24.840 --> 00:04:26.550
Next time, tie a rope to yourself!

00:04:27.010 --> 00:04:27.930
Fine, I will.

00:04:29.720 --> 00:04:31.020
Hey, Natsu!

00:04:31.100 --> 00:04:32.060
The same goes for you!

00:04:32.140 --> 00:04:33.850
Don't just go off on your own!

00:04:33.940 --> 00:04:35.600
You almost had me worried.

00:04:35.940 --> 00:04:37.730
I'm sorry.

00:04:38.730 --> 00:04:40.940
So, how did it go? Did you do your best?

00:04:41.110 --> 00:04:42.030
Yes.

00:04:43.110 --> 00:04:45.110
That's good. Nice work. Well done.

00:04:45.450 --> 00:04:46.860
You did it.

00:04:48.830 --> 00:04:52.700
Did you think I would actually say that?
You bumbling turtle!

00:04:52.790 --> 00:04:54.210
Don't get full of yourself!

00:04:54.290 --> 00:04:55.750
All of the doors here go down.

00:04:56.370 --> 00:04:58.250
Those guys sure are a nuisance.

00:04:58.540 --> 00:04:59.960
They're always like that.

00:05:01.590 --> 00:05:02.550
Ryo.

00:05:02.630 --> 00:05:03.630
What?

00:05:03.800 --> 00:05:05.220
Arashi asked me a question.

00:05:05.760 --> 00:05:08.470
He wanted to know
why I didn't run away back then.

00:05:08.550 --> 00:05:10.680
Yes. I heard it all.

00:05:10.760 --> 00:05:13.600
Tell me, Ryo. Did you ever think about

00:05:14.100 --> 00:05:16.100
running away from that test
without ever taking it?

00:05:16.390 --> 00:05:17.650
Of course, I didn't.

00:05:17.900 --> 00:05:19.400
That wasn't an option.

00:05:20.020 --> 00:05:21.270
<i>But it was an option,</i>

00:05:21.570 --> 00:05:22.980
<i>that final test we took.</i>

00:05:23.610 --> 00:05:24.780
<i>I knew about it.</i>

00:05:25.400 --> 00:05:28.110
<i>I knew everyone would be killed
except for the chosen seven.</i>

00:05:28.780 --> 00:05:31.530
<i>I could have warned them about that fact.</i>

00:05:32.290 --> 00:05:33.330
<i>But...</i>

00:05:33.410 --> 00:05:37.120
Hey, don't start finding new ways
to blame yourself for it.

00:05:39.040 --> 00:05:42.840
We'll never know what we could have done
or how it would have changed.

00:05:43.420 --> 00:05:44.630
We're already here anyway.

00:05:46.800 --> 00:05:47.930
You're right.

00:05:50.680 --> 00:05:52.100
We finally found a way up.

00:05:52.310 --> 00:05:54.520
Was this being stored away?

00:05:55.020 --> 00:05:56.430
Someone must have used it.

00:05:56.520 --> 00:05:58.850
Ango, your right hand.

00:05:59.270 --> 00:06:00.560
You can move your fingers again.

00:06:01.400 --> 00:06:03.360
Yes, that's right.

00:06:04.320 --> 00:06:06.610
I think Shigeru healed them for me.

00:06:06.690 --> 00:06:09.110
In a way, it was Arashi's doing.

00:06:10.570 --> 00:06:13.030
I thought he was just a dope,

00:06:13.120 --> 00:06:16.000
so it startled me
when he made such a sound argument.

00:06:16.660 --> 00:06:18.500
He was just like Hana, somehow.

00:06:18.580 --> 00:06:19.670
So are you.

00:06:19.750 --> 00:06:20.790
In what way?

00:06:20.880 --> 00:06:22.290
Have you forgotten?

00:06:22.920 --> 00:06:28.340
You were also an annoying jerk
who always made sound arguments.

00:06:28.880 --> 00:06:30.930
That's what upset you most
about Hana, right?

00:06:31.720 --> 00:06:34.010
She piqued your interest
even before you knew

00:06:34.350 --> 00:06:35.930
that she was Prof. Takashi's daughter.

00:06:37.020 --> 00:06:39.690
She rubbed you the wrong way,
but she also interested you.

00:06:42.560 --> 00:06:43.980
You're just going to ignore me?

00:06:44.520 --> 00:06:46.280
Hey! Come over this way!

00:06:49.030 --> 00:06:51.160
Did you hear something
from below just now?

00:06:51.240 --> 00:06:52.200
Yes.

00:06:58.580 --> 00:06:59.710
Oh, my.

00:07:01.170 --> 00:07:03.290
Wow! Big Sis!

00:07:03.380 --> 00:07:05.500
Ms. Botan! And Hotaru!

00:07:05.590 --> 00:07:06.920
Thank goodness you're all okay.

00:07:07.000 --> 00:07:08.920
We had a lot of trouble!

00:07:09.010 --> 00:07:10.880
We played ping pong
and then the elevator fell.

00:07:10.970 --> 00:07:14.050
We got washed away by a flood,
then fell and found turtles.

00:07:14.260 --> 00:07:15.430
We collected soybeans!

00:07:15.510 --> 00:07:17.390
We had Natsu pick us up with a crane!

00:07:17.470 --> 00:07:20.140
I have no idea
what you boys are trying to say.

00:07:20.520 --> 00:07:21.810
Please, just calm down.

00:07:22.850 --> 00:07:25.150
First, I'm glad that you're back with us,
Arashi.

00:07:25.570 --> 00:07:27.280
I thought we would never see you again.

00:07:27.940 --> 00:07:28.860
I'm sorry.

00:07:32.700 --> 00:07:35.950
It's good that the time for you to talk
finally came.

00:07:39.620 --> 00:07:42.000
Listen up, everyone.
There's something you should know.

00:07:44.920 --> 00:07:49.460
You mean the captain fired missiles
that were targeted at his own country?

00:07:50.130 --> 00:07:52.340
He said they even included
a nuclear missile.

00:07:52.930 --> 00:07:56.850
For one reason or another, the countdown
was stopped before it could finish.

00:07:57.310 --> 00:08:00.730
But after we arrived,
it seems to have started up once again.

00:08:01.230 --> 00:08:02.350
You're kidding.

00:08:02.560 --> 00:08:05.190
On top of that,
this ship is set to self-destruct.

00:08:05.730 --> 00:08:08.820
Then, perhaps that thing was
actually a missile.

00:08:08.900 --> 00:08:10.360
Did you see one, Natsu?

00:08:10.940 --> 00:08:11.940
Yes.

00:08:12.030 --> 00:08:14.700
So then, "time remaining" means...

00:08:14.780 --> 00:08:15.870
That's right.

00:08:16.200 --> 00:08:18.990
I assume you've seen
the monitors that say that.

00:08:19.330 --> 00:08:22.330
Apparently, it's the time remaining
until the missiles launch.

00:08:22.910 --> 00:08:24.540
Look, there's one here too.

00:08:24.620 --> 00:08:26.630
There are seven hours left?

00:08:26.710 --> 00:08:27.920
What do we do?

00:08:28.000 --> 00:08:29.590
We have three options.

00:08:29.670 --> 00:08:32.550
The first one is,
we leave this ship immediately.

00:08:32.840 --> 00:08:35.930
We get as far away as possible
to avoid being caught in the explosion.

00:08:36.010 --> 00:08:37.260
That won't work.

00:08:37.350 --> 00:08:40.100
Our ship is stuck in
the liquid concrete algae and can't move.

00:08:40.220 --> 00:08:42.100
Right. That's a problem.

00:08:42.770 --> 00:08:45.850
Our second option is to find a way
to stop the missile launch.

00:08:46.190 --> 00:08:47.610
Fortunately, there's still time.

00:08:47.940 --> 00:08:50.440
We can try our best to stop the missiles
before they launch.

00:08:51.070 --> 00:08:52.320
And the third option?

00:08:52.400 --> 00:08:54.820
Blow up the ship and let it sink.

00:08:55.070 --> 00:08:57.990
However, it's dangerous to do that
from the inside.

00:08:58.740 --> 00:09:01.870
It might be possible if we could rig
a timed explosive device.

00:09:02.120 --> 00:09:03.160
No good!

00:09:03.250 --> 00:09:06.290
Even if we did that, we would get caught
in the blast since our ship can't move.

00:09:06.370 --> 00:09:07.500
Exactly.

00:09:07.580 --> 00:09:10.840
Not to mention, who knows
what the missiles might do then?

00:09:10.920 --> 00:09:12.000
Let's stop the launch.

00:09:12.300 --> 00:09:14.170
There are people in Japan even now.

00:09:14.760 --> 00:09:18.140
Teams Autumn,
Spring, and Summer A are there.

00:09:19.390 --> 00:09:22.430
There may be other people
around somewhere too.

00:09:23.020 --> 00:09:25.100
<i>Hana is out there. Somewhere.</i>

00:09:25.180 --> 00:09:26.940
We have to stop it no matter what!

00:09:27.020 --> 00:09:31.270
There are plants and animals
thriving in the current environment too.

00:09:31.360 --> 00:09:32.570
That's for sure.

00:09:32.780 --> 00:09:36.360
Since we accidentally got onto this ship,
it started functioning again,

00:09:36.700 --> 00:09:38.360
so we need to handle it.

00:09:38.450 --> 00:09:41.030
And a nuclear missile means
a deadly nuclear fallout too!

00:09:41.120 --> 00:09:42.950
We'll end up dead even if we're far away!

00:09:43.120 --> 00:09:45.330
We would still be in danger
if we ran away, right?

00:09:45.410 --> 00:09:47.540
You're right. So then...

00:09:48.710 --> 00:09:50.920
Let's start working
to try and stop the missile launch.

00:09:51.500 --> 00:09:53.340
Actually, we just found a lead on that.

00:09:53.590 --> 00:09:55.550
I think this is probably
how we should do it.

00:09:56.090 --> 00:09:59.430
There are devices used to
manually cancel the launch.

00:09:59.890 --> 00:10:03.970
This ship is split up into four blocks,
A, B, C, and D.

00:10:04.220 --> 00:10:06.730
In each one of those
is a cancellation device.

00:10:07.810 --> 00:10:10.480
It's not clear whether
only one device will be enough,

00:10:10.610 --> 00:10:13.610
or if we have to use all of them
to successfully cancel it.

00:10:14.480 --> 00:10:17.490
The fact they are numbered one
through four seems significant.

00:10:18.070 --> 00:10:20.910
Then, for the time being,
we should go to the first device.

00:10:21.070 --> 00:10:22.330
We can figure it out from there.

00:10:22.410 --> 00:10:25.950
We also discovered it's possible
to communicate within the ship.

00:10:26.250 --> 00:10:30.120
I think there are intercoms
spread all throughout the ship.

00:10:30.210 --> 00:10:32.290
We should be able to use them
to maintain contact.

00:10:32.380 --> 00:10:33.290
All right.

00:10:33.380 --> 00:10:34.250
I'm going with you.

00:10:34.340 --> 00:10:35.380
No, Ryo.

00:10:35.630 --> 00:10:38.340
If we stop the launch,
the ship's power might possibly fail.

00:10:39.050 --> 00:10:41.550
I want you to secure us
a route out of here before then.

00:10:42.140 --> 00:10:44.430
Find a path that we can navigate
even in the dark.

00:10:44.930 --> 00:10:45.890
Roger that.

00:10:45.970 --> 00:10:47.310
Someone else come with me.

00:10:47.890 --> 00:10:48.850
I'll go.

00:10:49.600 --> 00:10:50.940
I'll go too!

00:10:51.270 --> 00:10:52.860
Do your best out there, Nat!

00:10:52.980 --> 00:10:54.650
I'm going to stick with Ryo too.

00:10:54.730 --> 00:10:56.860
-There's one more problem.
-What?

00:10:57.440 --> 00:10:58.360
The bacteria.

00:10:59.030 --> 00:11:02.240
They are propagating even faster,
and it's abnormally fast.

00:11:02.570 --> 00:11:04.410
What is that? It sounds gross.

00:11:04.700 --> 00:11:06.370
It's bacteria that eats iron.

00:11:06.790 --> 00:11:09.710
They might cause something
to go wrong with the ship's systems.

00:11:09.790 --> 00:11:12.670
Simply put,
this ship is a whole mess of danger.

00:11:12.750 --> 00:11:15.130
That's exactly right.
Everyone, be careful.

00:11:15.340 --> 00:11:16.250
Ango.

00:11:16.880 --> 00:11:18.050
You okay?

00:11:18.130 --> 00:11:19.420
I'm fine.

00:11:22.340 --> 00:11:23.760
"Ango. You okay?"

00:11:24.470 --> 00:11:25.430
How sweet.

00:11:25.510 --> 00:11:26.390
What?

00:11:26.470 --> 00:11:27.520
Your love for Ango.

00:11:27.640 --> 00:11:28.850
I don't know what you mean.

00:11:29.390 --> 00:11:31.270
I have always relied upon him.

00:11:31.690 --> 00:11:35.150
I knew he would handle being the leader
and the other annoying stuff.

00:11:35.480 --> 00:11:38.280
I need him to keep it together
or it will cause me trouble.

00:11:38.570 --> 00:11:39.400
That's all.

00:11:41.030 --> 00:11:42.740
Oh, Ryochin.

00:11:42.990 --> 00:11:43.950
I think I like you.

00:11:45.570 --> 00:11:46.660
<i>Ippon!</i>

00:11:46.740 --> 00:11:47.870
Is he a black belt?

00:11:48.080 --> 00:11:49.370
Are you all right?

00:11:51.460 --> 00:11:53.750
If you're heading for the exit,
then I will accompany you.

00:11:54.380 --> 00:11:56.340
Semimaru,
I want you to stay here with Hotaru.

00:11:56.420 --> 00:11:57.590
Sure.

00:11:58.670 --> 00:12:00.550
<i>Ango's group, can you hear me?</i>

00:12:01.050 --> 00:12:03.930
<i>If you find an intercom,
try talking into it.</i>

00:12:07.140 --> 00:12:08.470
Is this one?

00:12:08.560 --> 00:12:09.680
<i>Hello?</i>

00:12:10.220 --> 00:12:11.270
We hear you, Natsu.

00:12:12.230 --> 00:12:13.730
It even shows us where you are.

00:12:14.440 --> 00:12:18.320
<i>Go straight and then cross two passages
that shifted vertically,</i>

00:12:18.480 --> 00:12:19.860
<i>then go down at the next corner.</i>

00:12:20.360 --> 00:12:21.320
Amazing.

00:12:21.400 --> 00:12:23.200
I didn't realize that's how it worked.

00:12:23.530 --> 00:12:26.120
<i>That's right. Be more alert.</i>

00:12:26.660 --> 00:12:28.530
<i>Learn how to traverse this ship.</i>

00:12:29.490 --> 00:12:32.620
Okay, Arashi, Natsu.
Watch your step and let's move.

00:12:32.830 --> 00:12:33.790
-Right!
-Right!

00:12:34.870 --> 00:12:37.670
The entrance that we came in through is
just up ahead.

00:12:38.210 --> 00:12:39.250
Around the corner.

00:12:40.090 --> 00:12:41.550
It must be dark outside already.

00:12:41.960 --> 00:12:43.340
I would love some fresh air.

00:12:43.420 --> 00:12:44.590
Is this it?

00:12:45.260 --> 00:12:48.510
What is this? A fire door? A bulkhead?

00:12:48.720 --> 00:12:50.560
It looks super thick.

00:12:50.640 --> 00:12:51.720
When did this happen?

00:12:52.220 --> 00:12:54.560
Was it built to keep
the passengers trapped?

00:12:54.940 --> 00:12:56.940
To prevent anyone from escaping
the self-destruct?

00:12:57.440 --> 00:13:00.230
This ship was set up
to deal with any enemy imaginable,

00:13:00.860 --> 00:13:04.030
to prevent it from being stolen
or even taken over.

00:13:04.820 --> 00:13:08.820
If the worst happened,
they could seal it off and self-destruct.

00:13:10.240 --> 00:13:13.250
Hey, Ryo, what about the door
we came in through?

00:13:13.330 --> 00:13:16.080
I doubt we can use it either,
but let's check it out.

00:13:16.710 --> 00:13:19.790
<i>Semimaru, Hotaru.
The entrance we came in is sealed off.</i>

00:13:19.880 --> 00:13:21.170
What? No way!

00:13:21.300 --> 00:13:22.550
<i>We're going to look for another.</i>

00:13:23.590 --> 00:13:25.260
<i>We've reached our destination.</i>

00:13:26.760 --> 00:13:28.390
We heard what Botan said about the exit.

00:13:28.680 --> 00:13:32.060
I guess that means stopping
the missiles is our only option.

00:13:32.600 --> 00:13:34.810
We're going to look inside now
and report back.

00:13:43.150 --> 00:13:44.570
A terminal.

00:13:44.780 --> 00:13:47.910
If it asks for an ID or a password,
then we're in trouble.

00:13:47.990 --> 00:13:49.990
I don't know anything
about how those work.

00:13:50.070 --> 00:13:51.030
You do it, Arashi.

00:13:51.120 --> 00:13:52.910
<i>There is a monitor inside.</i>

00:13:53.200 --> 00:13:54.830
Okay, Natsu. Keep up the good work.

00:13:55.500 --> 00:13:58.170
Make it so we can always hear you.

00:13:58.790 --> 00:14:01.130
<i>Ms. Botan's team, please listen as well.</i>

00:14:04.260 --> 00:14:06.510
First, let's see if the power works.

00:14:10.050 --> 00:14:13.510
BOOTING

00:14:13.600 --> 00:14:15.020
Q: WHAT IS YOUR FAVORITE BOOK?

00:14:15.100 --> 00:14:16.100
My favorite book?

00:14:16.480 --> 00:14:17.980
There's no way we could know that.

00:14:18.350 --> 00:14:20.600
<i>Arashi, "The Rime of the Ancient Mariner."</i>

00:14:20.850 --> 00:14:24.360
<i>The kanji are, "old," "sailor," and "go."
Try entering that.</i>

00:14:24.530 --> 00:14:26.650
<i>The captain quoted that poem
at the end of his message.</i>

00:14:26.740 --> 00:14:28.320
Thank you, Ms. Botan.

00:14:29.660 --> 00:14:33.830
<i>It's about a ship's captain who kills
an albatross without reason and is cursed.</i>

00:14:33.910 --> 00:14:37.750
Eventually, he ends up wandering
on a journey of atonement.

00:14:38.750 --> 00:14:41.040
It's a major poem
written by an English poet.

00:14:41.130 --> 00:14:42.590
THE RIME OF THE ANCIENT MARNIER
ENTER

00:14:42.670 --> 00:14:43.670
IDENTITY CONFIRMED

00:14:43.750 --> 00:14:44.750
That worked!

00:14:44.840 --> 00:14:46.090
ENTER THE SAME CODE AS BEFORE.

00:14:46.170 --> 00:14:48.470
A code? That figures.

00:14:49.430 --> 00:14:50.760
"Same as before"?

00:14:50.840 --> 00:14:55.350
Hotaru, do you know the procedure
they used to engage the missile launch?

00:14:56.180 --> 00:14:58.520
Can you take a look at the manual
for this device again?

00:14:58.600 --> 00:15:00.730
To engage the launch, not cancel it?

00:15:00.810 --> 00:15:01.730
<i>Yes.</i>

00:15:03.610 --> 00:15:04.520
I found it.

00:15:04.820 --> 00:15:06.860
"For launch and self-destruct,

00:15:06.940 --> 00:15:10.110
the approval of at least four people,
including the captain, is necessary."

00:15:10.200 --> 00:15:11.860
That explains the four booths.

00:15:12.110 --> 00:15:15.830
<i>"Each one has a question
that's used to confirm their identity."</i>

00:15:16.040 --> 00:15:17.040
I see.

00:15:17.540 --> 00:15:21.000
<i>"After each of them decides
and enters an eight-digit code,</i>

00:15:21.120 --> 00:15:23.130
<i>they have to simultaneously hold down</i>

00:15:23.210 --> 00:15:25.290
<i>the activation button
for at least three seconds."</i>

00:15:26.170 --> 00:15:27.670
It also explains how to cancel it!

00:15:28.260 --> 00:15:30.470
<i>"Input the same code
that was established previously."</i>

00:15:30.670 --> 00:15:32.380
<i>Then it's the same
as the launch procedure.</i>

00:15:32.470 --> 00:15:35.760
Basically, we have to find the codes
the four of them made

00:15:36.060 --> 00:15:38.180
and then hit the cancel button
simultaneously.

00:15:38.270 --> 00:15:39.140
<i>Correct.</i>

00:15:39.220 --> 00:15:43.480
Based on that last question, the captain
set the code for this terminal.

00:15:43.650 --> 00:15:45.810
Hotaru, give us directions
to the Captain's Quarters.

00:15:46.110 --> 00:15:47.610
<i>Go to block A-1-6.</i>

00:15:49.740 --> 00:15:51.280
I hope we can find some clues.

00:15:51.570 --> 00:15:52.490
Yes.

00:15:52.570 --> 00:15:54.370
No, hold up.

00:15:54.780 --> 00:15:58.950
Even if we figure out the captain's code,
what will we do about the other three?

00:16:00.790 --> 00:16:02.250
Start looking for something.

00:16:02.790 --> 00:16:04.170
Arashi, you check out the terminal.

00:16:04.750 --> 00:16:05.790
Okay.

00:16:08.630 --> 00:16:10.300
FINAL DAY: TIME REMAINING

00:16:14.640 --> 00:16:17.970
Maybe he left a note in his pocket
or something.

00:16:18.760 --> 00:16:22.020
But even if he did,
I doubt we could pull it out of this.

00:16:22.100 --> 00:16:23.310
Is that platinum?

00:16:23.730 --> 00:16:24.730
It hasn't corroded.

00:16:26.860 --> 00:16:28.520
Arashi. Ango.

00:16:30.650 --> 00:16:31.820
We found it!

00:16:37.910 --> 00:16:39.330
ENTER THE SAME CODE AS BEFORE

00:16:39.410 --> 00:16:40.330
CODE CONFIRMED

00:16:40.410 --> 00:16:41.870
It worked, Natsu!

00:16:41.950 --> 00:16:43.910
-Okay, let's head for number two!
-Okay!

00:16:44.000 --> 00:16:45.710
You pulled it off? Really?

00:16:45.920 --> 00:16:47.330
That's one down.

00:16:47.420 --> 00:16:49.170
<i>We cleared the first booth.</i>

00:16:49.250 --> 00:16:50.420
Really?

00:16:52.510 --> 00:16:54.090
The problem is,

00:16:54.340 --> 00:16:57.800
aside from the captain, we have no way
to identify who the others were.

00:16:58.760 --> 00:17:00.510
We have no clues to find the codes.

00:17:00.600 --> 00:17:02.180
BOOTING

00:17:02.270 --> 00:17:03.520
Q: WHAT IS THE NAME OF YOUR PET?

00:17:04.100 --> 00:17:05.020
<i>Could this be...</i>

00:17:05.100 --> 00:17:08.440
How in the world should we know
who they're asking?

00:17:08.560 --> 00:17:09.610
Right.

00:17:09.690 --> 00:17:11.900
Mimi... It's Mimi!

00:17:14.700 --> 00:17:16.610
IDENTITY CONFIRMED
ENTER THE SAME CODE AS BEFORE.

00:17:16.700 --> 00:17:17.610
That's amazing, Natsu!

00:17:17.950 --> 00:17:20.030
I found a framed picture
of a cat named Mimi.

00:17:20.580 --> 00:17:23.450
The code might be
where I found the picture.

00:17:24.200 --> 00:17:25.790
We might find it if we go there.

00:17:26.290 --> 00:17:27.120
Let's go!

00:17:29.960 --> 00:17:31.880
FINAL DAY: TIME REMAINING

00:17:32.340 --> 00:17:35.010
Hey, what do you think about splitting up?

00:17:35.340 --> 00:17:38.640
You guys go to the other terminals,
numbers three and four.

00:17:38.720 --> 00:17:39.720
Natsu?

00:17:39.800 --> 00:17:42.180
It's okay. I can go on my own.

00:17:42.260 --> 00:17:44.350
All right,
then you take care of number two.

00:17:44.730 --> 00:17:46.140
Natsu, let's stop those missiles!

00:17:47.310 --> 00:17:48.400
I'm going too!

00:17:48.480 --> 00:17:50.480
Booth three is the closest one.

00:17:50.690 --> 00:17:51.860
Okay, that's where I'm going!

00:17:53.400 --> 00:17:58.700
<i>Semimaru is going to number three,
so you two should head for number four.</i>

00:17:59.570 --> 00:18:02.080
Are you going to be okay all alone,
Semimaru?

00:18:02.160 --> 00:18:05.870
There's no way I'm going to take it easy
when even Natsu is doing her best!

00:18:05.950 --> 00:18:08.210
We need to hurry and find an exit as well.

00:18:10.040 --> 00:18:11.790
BOOTING

00:18:11.920 --> 00:18:12.960
Arashi,

00:18:13.050 --> 00:18:14.760
what do you want to eat most right now?

00:18:15.010 --> 00:18:16.470
For me, it's curry and rice.

00:18:16.720 --> 00:18:18.800
<i>Right, I think it's the same for me.</i>

00:18:18.880 --> 00:18:20.760
I would have to say seafood curry.

00:18:20.840 --> 00:18:22.640
Chicken curry, medium spicy for me.

00:18:22.890 --> 00:18:26.060
I would love some green curry
or coconut milk curry.

00:18:26.310 --> 00:18:27.940
With tons of thick-cut vegetables.

00:18:28.730 --> 00:18:31.190
Personally,
I don't like thick-cut vegetables.

00:18:31.270 --> 00:18:33.230
Especially the big chunks of potatoes.

00:18:33.320 --> 00:18:35.150
Yes! I'm the same way!

00:18:35.320 --> 00:18:38.650
With big potato chunks,
I think it ruins the flavor of the curry.

00:18:39.280 --> 00:18:41.570
Ango, did your group ever eat curry?

00:18:42.070 --> 00:18:45.080
We made it often. Everyone liked it.

00:18:45.160 --> 00:18:47.040
<i>We made a big pot of it when camping.</i>

00:18:47.120 --> 00:18:49.120
Okay. We all think curry, Semimaru.

00:18:50.960 --> 00:18:52.880
IDENTITY CONFIRMED
ENTER THE SAME CODE AS BEFORE.

00:18:53.130 --> 00:18:54.250
That was right!

00:18:54.380 --> 00:18:56.550
Arashi, I'm going to head for the kitchen.

00:18:56.920 --> 00:19:00.300
This terminal was probably the chef's.
I bet he left a note in the fridge.

00:19:03.800 --> 00:19:07.060
They had a big shootout in here.
It's full of holes.

00:19:07.140 --> 00:19:09.560
Does the terminal still work?

00:19:10.440 --> 00:19:12.310
Come on. Please work.

00:19:14.060 --> 00:19:16.650
BOOTING

00:19:17.900 --> 00:19:20.150
"What sport can't you play
inside of this ship?"

00:19:20.240 --> 00:19:21.320
<i>Sport?</i>

00:19:21.410 --> 00:19:23.490
"Please choose one of the following.

00:19:24.410 --> 00:19:29.660
Soccer, basketball, bowling,
golf, tennis, baseball."

00:19:30.250 --> 00:19:32.080
A sport you can't play in the ship?

00:19:32.170 --> 00:19:35.880
They had a ping pong table
and a basketball hoop and stuff, right?

00:19:35.960 --> 00:19:39.170
Right, there was a room
that was like a gym.

00:19:39.510 --> 00:19:41.840
In the storage room,
I found volleyballs and golf clubs.

00:19:42.340 --> 00:19:43.720
Then the answer is baseball.

00:19:44.470 --> 00:19:47.180
I didn't find any bats
or baseballs in there.

00:19:54.770 --> 00:19:57.900
So, you offed yourself after you
hit the switch to launch the missiles?

00:19:58.780 --> 00:20:00.940
Sorry, but we're going to stop them.

00:20:01.860 --> 00:20:03.820
<i>Semimaru, baseball was the right answer!</i>

00:20:05.200 --> 00:20:06.910
<i>Semimaru? What's wrong?</i>

00:20:07.370 --> 00:20:09.410
Well, I found the code I was looking for.

00:20:09.700 --> 00:20:10.580
<i>Nice work!</i>

00:20:12.960 --> 00:20:15.580
I'm sure you must have made
delicious curry.

00:20:17.460 --> 00:20:18.750
<i>I'm not scared.</i>

00:20:19.210 --> 00:20:23.050
<i>I was scared out of my wits at first,
but now I don't feel any fear at all.</i>

00:20:23.630 --> 00:20:26.600
<i>In fact, I can feel courage
welling up inside of me.</i>

00:20:26.890 --> 00:20:28.810
<i>Natsu, how about on your end?</i>

00:20:28.890 --> 00:20:29.770
<i>You still alive?</i>

00:20:31.060 --> 00:20:32.890
I'm fine. I made it to the place.

00:20:33.190 --> 00:20:34.560
I'm going to search for it now.

00:20:37.900 --> 00:20:41.280
No luck. If it fell off
and rolled somewhere, then...

00:20:46.240 --> 00:20:47.570
I found it!

00:20:47.870 --> 00:20:48.830
<i>Wow!</i>

00:20:48.910 --> 00:20:49.830
<i>Good job!</i>

00:20:53.290 --> 00:20:54.580
MIMI

00:20:54.670 --> 00:20:57.130
Mimi is very cute.

00:20:57.500 --> 00:20:59.800
I'm sure you must have
taken very good care of her.

00:21:00.800 --> 00:21:02.050
<i>Be careful on your way back.</i>

00:21:02.840 --> 00:21:03.800
Right!

00:21:06.760 --> 00:21:08.180
There are too many things in here.

00:21:15.060 --> 00:21:16.230
I found it!

00:21:18.730 --> 00:21:20.270
How did you know it would be there?

00:21:20.770 --> 00:21:23.440
I figured they really loved baseball.

00:21:24.150 --> 00:21:28.320
So, they must have had
some precious baseball memento.

00:21:28.410 --> 00:21:30.120
Is that so?

00:21:31.030 --> 00:21:33.330
Ango, please return to booth number one.

00:21:33.750 --> 00:21:35.460
I'm going to go to number four.

00:21:35.750 --> 00:21:37.790
Let's stop the missiles no matter what!

00:21:38.750 --> 00:21:39.630
Arashi.

00:21:39.710 --> 00:21:40.590
Yes?

00:21:40.670 --> 00:21:42.840
Nothing. Just be careful out there.

00:21:42.920 --> 00:21:43.960
You too, Ango.

00:21:45.630 --> 00:21:48.050
<i>I never would have picked up on
a person's feelings like that.</i>

00:21:48.340 --> 00:21:52.180
<i>But as a member of Summer B,
you were able to.</i>

00:21:55.270 --> 00:21:58.190
FINAL DAY: TIME REMAINING

00:21:58.270 --> 00:22:00.520
Okay, everyone, are you ready?

00:22:00.610 --> 00:22:01.610
Yes.

00:22:01.690 --> 00:22:03.320
-Yes.
-Sure.

00:22:04.690 --> 00:22:05.990
Let's do it, Hotaru.

00:22:06.490 --> 00:22:10.160
When I count down to zero,
hold down the button for three seconds.

00:22:10.620 --> 00:22:12.370
All right, here we go.

00:22:12.870 --> 00:22:13.740
Five.

00:22:13.830 --> 00:22:14.750
Four.

00:22:14.830 --> 00:22:15.750
<i>Three.</i>

00:22:15.830 --> 00:22:16.750
<i>Two.</i>

00:22:16.830 --> 00:22:17.750
<i>One.</i>

00:22:17.830 --> 00:22:19.000
<i>Zero.</i>

00:22:23.300 --> 00:22:27.420
FINAL DAY: TIME REMAINING

00:22:29.090 --> 00:22:30.140
It won't stop.
